    "q-92248": {
      "dom_id": "step-q92248",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $15\\,|\\,32b$ then $15\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${7}^{2}\\,|\\,7b$ then ${7}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,25b$ then $9\\,|\\,b$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(15,32)=1.$ Therefore, we have $15\\,|\\,32b$ and $\\text{gcd}(15,32)=1,$ which implies $15\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=7.$ Then, ${7}^{2}∣7\\cdot 7$ but ${7}^{2}∤7.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},25)=1.$ Therefore, we have ${3}^{2}∣25b$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},25)=1,$ which implies ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
