    "q-93650": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93650",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,19b$ then ${19}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $12\\,|\\,35b$ then $12\\,|\\,b$\n- If $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ then $22\\,|\\,b$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let $b=19.$ Then, ${19}^{2}∣19\\cdot 19$ but ${19}^{2}∤19.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1.$ Therefore, we have $12\\,|\\,35b$ and $\\text{gcd}(12,35)=1,$ which implies $12\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1.$ Therefore, we have $22\\,|\\,{7}^{2}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(22,{7}^{2})=1,$ which implies $22\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
