    "q-93648": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93648",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ then ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,17b$ then ${17}^{2}\\,|\\,b$\n- If $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ then $20\\,|\\,b$",
      "worked_solution": "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$c\\,|\\,ab\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,c)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $\\,c\\,|\\,b.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1.$ Therefore, we have ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,10b$ and $\\text{gcd}({3}^{2},10)=1,$ which implies ${3}^{2}\\,|\\,b.$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=17.$ Then, ${17}^{2}∣17\\cdot 17$ but ${17}^{2}∤17.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1.$ Therefore, we have $20\\,|\\,{3}^{3}b$ and $\\text{gcd}(20,{3}^{3})=1,$ which implies $20\\,|\\,b.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
