    "q-93657": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93657",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $3\\,|\\,a$ and $2\\,|\\,a$ then $6\\,|\\,a$\n- If $7\\,|\\,b$ and $14\\,|\\,b$ then $98\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${2}^{3}\\,|\\,c$ and $3\\,|\\,c$ then $24\\,|\\,c$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1$ and $2\\cdot 3=6.$ Therefore, we have $(2\\,|\\,a),(3\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(2,3)=1,$ which implies $(6\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, let $b=14.$ Then, $(7∣14)$ and $(14∣14),$ but $(98∤14).$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1$ and ${2}^{3}\\cdot 3=24.$ Therefore, we have $({2}^{3}\\,|\\,c),(3\\,|\\,c),$ and $\\text{gcd}({2}^{3},3)=1,$ which implies $(24\\,|\\,c).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
