    "q-93658": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93658",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $4\\,|\\,a$ and $9\\,|\\,a$ then $36\\,|\\,a$\n- If $5\\,|\\,b$ and $7\\,|\\,b$ then $35\\,|\\,b$\n- If ${6}^{2}\\,|\\,c$ and $2\\,|\\,c$ then $72\\,|\\,c$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$\n\n$a\\,|\\,c,$ $\\,b\\,|\\,c,\\,$ and $\\,\\text{gcd}(a,b)=1$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $ab\\,|\\,c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1$ and $4\\cdot 9=36.$ Therefore, we have $(4\\,|\\,a),(9\\,|\\,a),$ and $\\text{gcd}(4,9)=1,$ which implies $(36\\,|\\,a).$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1$ and $5\\cdot 7=35.$ Therefore, we have $(5\\,|\\,b),(7\\,|\\,b),$ and $\\text{gcd}(5,7)=1,$ which implies $(35\\,|\\,b).$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $c=36.$ Then, $({6}^{2}∣36)$ and $(2∣36),$ but $(72∤36).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
